WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.400
 An

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.668
extraordinary look,

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.536
rarely seen at the moment

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.538
when a Russian fighter jet collided

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.107
with a US drone.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:07.941
The US military

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.909
just put out this video today

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.344
and in this we'll show you

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.812
it goes out of communication a bit.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.147
But take a look at this still shot.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:14.948
You can see

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.149
one of the things that the government,

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.550
the Pentagon has laid out.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.718
The Russian fighter jet

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.487
just dumping the U.S.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.622
dumping fuel at one shot.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.090
And then Russia has denied

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.058
that the collision

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.793
that it collided with the drone.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.495
But in these side by side

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.562
photos, you can see that

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.631
the drones propeller has been damaged.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.333
And you can see through the video

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.268
from the collision you see right there.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.002
Let's get over to Oren

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.670
Liebermann, who's live at the Pentagon,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.873
because not only is this video

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.474
the fact that we are seeing it

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.009
extraordinary, Oren,

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.511
but you also are learning some more

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.111
about what

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.480
Russian leadership knew about this.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:48.948
Absolutely.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.150
So first, let's take a video,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.817
a look at the video

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.152
to get a better sense of this.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.153
And there are two clips

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.421
here of two different passes

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.855
from those Russian fighter jets

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:56.623
as they approach

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.525
the US MQ nine Reaper drone.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.859
So here is the past

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.128
where they dump fuel as they get close

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.763
and in the first pass.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.832
The fighter jet doesn't hit the Russian

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.734
I'm sorry, the U.S. drone.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.002
And you can see the propeller

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.103
still spinning there.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.738
The propeller is working fine.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.872
It is the second clip

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.174
that makes it clearer

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.175
what happened here

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.142
and that the Russian denial

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.844
simply doesn't hold water.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.712
That jet approaches Again,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.182
a Russian Sukhoi su 27 fighter jet.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.583
And as it passes, it

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.185
once again dumps fuel

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.220
as it hits the drone.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.122
The video itself is disrupted

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.789
a little bit.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.291
Essentially, it's pixelated

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.525
and goes to bars for a moment.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.294
But when it comes back online,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.428
you can see

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.663
the damaged propeller,

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.430
a propeller, obviously

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:37.831
not supposed

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.165
to look like that with a bent.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.234
And that's the telling signal,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.702
the telling clip of video

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.070
where you see the collision

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.405
between the Russian fighter jet

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.573
or the effects of the collision,

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.374
I should say, between the Russian fighter

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.909
jet and the drone itself.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.711
Now, for more context on this,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.912
we have learned from two U.S.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.646
officials familiar

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.515
with the intelligence behind the matter

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.750
that the instructions to harass the drone

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.184
essentially

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:58.785
the orders

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.787
to the Russian fighter pilots came from

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.222
some of the highest levels

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:02.956
of the Russian

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.192
Ministry of Defense to harass, disturb,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.794
disrupt in some way

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.329
the operation of that U.S.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.497
surveillance drone.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.064
Those officials

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:11.865
say it's not clear

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.466
that it went higher than that.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.167
In other words,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.268
it's not clear that Russian

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.237
President Vladimir Putin knew in advance

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.538
this was going to happen.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.739
But it is telling

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.040
that the officials are telling us

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.509
that the highest levels

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.511
of the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.479
gave the orders to harass the U.S.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.981
drone over the black sea.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.982
The drone itself

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.583
then went down, according to U.S.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.017
Air Force

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.584
Europe,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.687
some 70 or 80 miles southwest of Crimea.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.856
Now for the follow on here,

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.091
the video itself

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.359
gives support to the U.S.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.894
side in the U.S.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.262
position and essentially narrative

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.029
of what happened here

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.264
and seriously undercuts

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:45.331
the Russian claims

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.634
that there had been no collision

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.735
which was what the U.S.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.836
or rather the Russian ambassador

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.236
to the U.S.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.271
said after he was summoned

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.338
to the State Department

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.007
on the day this story came out.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.808
Kate, we will continue to follow this.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.309
And, of course,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.844
to see this incredible video

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.646
of how this all played out.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.980
Absolutely. Great reporting, Oren.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.348
Thank you very much.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.349
For more on this.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.350
Let me bring in retired

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.685
Lieutenant General Ben Hodges.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.920
He's a former commander of U.S.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.288
Army Forces in Europe.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.656
General, thanks for coming in.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.058
19 passes made by the jets

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.060
going on for 30 to 40 minutes

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.261
is what we're learning.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.330
What sticks out to you in this video?

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.300
Well, two things.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.168
First of all, this obviously was

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.336
was not an accident.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.938
This was a deliberate act.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.973
And I think or did a good job of sort

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.509
of laying out the context for that.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.978
But what makes us important

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.781
is not the loss of a drone, but this is

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.549
this is what it means to defend

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.751
the so-called international rules

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.153
based order,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.421
international airspace,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.256
freedom of navigation, claims

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.390
to territorial waters.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:44.924
All of these

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.993
things are being played out now

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.094
because of Russia's

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.430
illegal annexation of Crimea

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.066
and their illegal war of aggression

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:53.900
against Ukraine.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.101
So this is a

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.603
symptom of this And,

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:56.970
of course,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.938
the Chinese will watch to see

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.773
how we respond to this as well

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.975
because of their own

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.677
illegal claims in the Pacific.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.646
What do you think of how?

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:07.113
What do you think

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.382
first of how the response

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.717
we have heard from the Pentagon,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.285
from the defense secretary,

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.786
from the chairman of the Joint

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.521
Chiefs, coming out very clearly

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:16.956
and talking about this now

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.624
a couple of times.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.394
Yeah, I've been impressed, actually,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:22.695
though,

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:23.296
Secretary

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.130
Ashton, of course,

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.232
conveying the seriousness of this,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.001
Chairman Milley,

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.969
but also not overreacting.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.037
This is not the kind of thing

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.439
where now we're going to go out and start

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.540
kinetic engagements

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.309
against Russian aircraft.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.511
Instead, what Secretary Austin said.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.113
All right.
We're going to put another drone

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:40.747
back up there.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.248
This is international airspace.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.249
We were doing everything

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.450
according to law.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.520
And so this is how you protect and defend

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.556
the use of international airspace,

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.624
which affects

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.860
all of us, not just there in and around

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.328
Ukraine.

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.496
It also is important,

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.930
I think, to see the example

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.931
of the United States

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.000
with transparency, immediately

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.702
releasing a video saying

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.670
this is what happened

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.371
and you and your team

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.606
there have done a good job

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.675
of making it clear what happened.

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.575
You can be sure those

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:10.943
two Russian aircraft

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.612
have video capability.

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.747
And if they were, in fact,

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:17.417
no not guilty of what it's clear

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.484
that they've done.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:18.951
No doubt

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.153
the Kremlin would have rolled out

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.255
that video immediately

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.222
to make their case.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.124
And we haven't seen any of that

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.126
One question is always, you know,

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.761
with every move, is there

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.396
is there a counter move from Russia?

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.565
Do you do you think,

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.000
though, important for transparency,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:34.367
as you say,

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.835
showing leadership and transparency

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.103
on the part of the Pentagon?

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:39.205
Do you think Russia will interpret this

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.708
and see a reason to further respond

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.309
now that this video has been put out?

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:45.745
I think

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.614
they will wait to see what we do next.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.182
Obviously,

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.184
I mean, this is the typical Kremlin

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.019
playbook of

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.722
deny everything distort, distract

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.825
to try and change the narrative.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.927
And of course, if we don't respond

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.062
by putting a drone up again,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:03.930
then this kind of

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.498
gives weight to their claim

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.800
that their airspace around Crimea

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.102
is actually theirs.

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:10.470
So we are correct

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.704
and the secretary is correct

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.173
to go back in and challenge that.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.410
But I think there's no need to overreact

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.579
or try to shoot something down.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.049
But we have to make sure we continue to

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.018
uphold freedom of navigation

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.421
and use of international airspace.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.590
And the as we see in

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.825
the video is Oren laid out very well.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.360
The video very clearly undercuts

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.195
Russia's denial,

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.597
though, a Russian strategy,

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:38.831
as you point to, General, that

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:40.199
the Russian jet,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:40.800
that the Russian jet

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.234
did, that

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.301
the incident didn't happen, that

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.070
the Russian jet didn't clip the drone.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.471
But what is still unclear

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.706
is whether the Russian pilots

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:48.808
intended to strike the drone.

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:51.844
Does the answer to that question matter?

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:53.946
Matter from your perspective?

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.015
Well,

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.018
this reflects exactly what John

00:06:59.018 --> 00:06:59.852
Kirby said

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.287
yesterday, that

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:03.723
this is a reckless, unprovoked personal

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.559
and unsafe act by the Russian pilots.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.294
I have not been impressed

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.096
over the past 14 months

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.230
with the
level of training

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.333
and discipline of Russian pilots It's

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:16.335
one thing to take off and land and

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.670
and fly close to something.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:18.204
But, I mean,

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:18.971
when you talk about

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.774
getting up next to another aircraft,

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.410
getting as close as they did there

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.412
with turbulence, things that can happen.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.116
The chances of a mistake are very high.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:31.684
And I think I don't know

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.820
that they intended to actually hit it.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.521
I'm sure that what they wanted to do

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.356
was cause it to fail

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.024
or to

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:39.725
disrupt the operation by dumping

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.127
fuel on it,

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.563
which in itself,

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:45.631
obviously, that was a deliberate act

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:46.999
to actually hit it.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.501
Of course, we don't know.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.002
But I mean, when you get that close,

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:50.937
those are the kind of things

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:51.571
that can happen.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:52.505
And again,

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:53.840
this is the same military

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.708
that is committing war crimes

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:57.410
every day in Ukraine.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.611
And it reflects,

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:01.314
I think, also a very brutal,

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.449
ruthless sort of society there.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.818
So I'm not surprised that their pilots

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.286
would be a reflection

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:09.722
of that in terms of undisciplined.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:10.789
Hmm.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:11.891
Lieutenant General Ben

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:12.992
Hodges, thank you very much.

